I'd have thought that the answer to this was obvious. As a player all 
you can do is set yourself a hard turn limit to play the game, which is 
a fairly boring challenge. The developers, on the other hand, could do 
something more interesting like adding the turn count/100000 to zlevel 
in rndmonst(), thereby slowly ratcheting up the monster difficulty on 
long games. Instead of setting a rather boring hard limit this presents 
the player with an interesting tradeoff problem to solve, and it isn't 
something the player (or most of them, anyway) can do for themselves.


